  data:  # fe3c
    kind: invariant  # fe3c
    title: "slice --out slice.json silently overridden by default-detection at cli.py:1377"  # fe3c
    status: violated  # fe3c
    priority: 2  # fe3c
    parent:  # fe3c
    tags:  # fe3c
    - dogfooding  # fe3c
    - pass7  # fe3c
    - cli_ux  # fe3c
    isbefore: []  # fe3c
    duplicate_of: []  # fe3c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fe3c
    pr_ref:  # fe3c
    description: ""  # fe3c
    fields:  # fe3c
      statement: "When the user explicitly passes '--out slice.json' to 'hypergumbo slice', the output must be written to that path. Currently it is silently redirected to a cache directory because the code at cli.py:1377 checks 'if out_path_arg == \"slice.json\"' to detect the argparse default and substitute a cache path."  # fe3c
      root_cause: "argparse default for --out is the literal string 'slice.json'. By the time cli.py:1377 runs, args.out == 'slice.json' regardless of whether the user typed it explicitly. The fix is to set the argparse default to None (or argparse.SUPPRESS) and substitute the default only when args.out is None. Reproduced with --out slice.json (overridden), --out=slice.json (overridden), --out plain.json (works), --out slice.x.json (works), --out slice.foo (works), --out myslice.json (works) — only the exact basename 'slice.json' triggers the bug."  # fe3c
